---
/**
 * Shrink My First Step — AI tool 2 (docs/decisions.md D9, D10, D11).
 *
 * This is the SHELL. The serverless function does not exist yet, so the page degrades
 * honestly: what it does, the input it will ask for, the shape of the answer, and a plain
 * statement that it is not live. Nothing else on the site depends on it.
 *
 * The tool is Chapter 1's third Play step turned into a machine, so the step it automates
 * is quoted here verbatim from the book rather than described.
 *
 * No <form> element — not because the CSP would stop one (the shipped policy is
 * form-action 'self', which permits the same-origin page-number form on / and /404), but
 * because an input that looks live and silently does nothing is worse than one that says
 * it is off.
 */
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import ChapterFurniture from "../../components/ChapterFurniture.astro";
import SafetyNotice from "../../components/SafetyNotice.astro";
import Box from "../../components/Box.astro";
import Flag from "../../components/Flag.astro";
import PageRef from "../../components/PageRef.astro";
import { allChapters, allRealityChecks } from "../../lib/content";
import { metaFor } from "../reality-check/_checks";

const chapter = (await allChapters()).find((c) => c.data.slug === "dream-big")!;
const step = chapter.data.play.find((p) => p.n === 3)!;
const check = (await allRealityChecks()).find((c) => c.id === "dream-big")!;
const checkMeta = metaFor(check.id);

/* Illustrative only, and labelled as such on the page. Deliberately not built from the
   book's Chapter 1 story: the 15 stories are the book's, not the site's (D4). */
const EXAMPLE_GOAL = "I want to start a YouTube channel.";
const EXAMPLE_STEPS = [
  {
    step: "Say the first sixty seconds of one video out loud and time it on your phone.",
    proof: "A script you have actually heard, and a real number for how long it runs.",
  },
  {
    step: "Film that sixty seconds in one take. Do not edit it, do not re-record it.",
    proof: "One video file with today's date on it, which did not exist this morning.",
  },
  {
    step: "Send the take to one person and ask what was confusing.",
    proof: "One reply with one specific note in it — the first outside information you have.",
  },
];
---

<Page
  title="Shrink My First Step"
  description="Type the goal that is too big and get three first steps that fit in 20 minutes, each with the proof it leaves behind. Chapter 1's third Play step, as a tool."
  printedPage={chapter.data.printedPage}
>
  <ChapterFurniture
    eyebrow={`AI tool · ${chapter.data.eyebrow.split(" / ")[0]}`}
    title="Shrink My First Step"
    subtitle="Type the goal that is too big. Get three first steps that fit in twenty minutes, and the proof each one leaves."
  />

  <SafetyNotice tone="crisis" />

  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="status" role="note">
      <span class="status__badge">Not live yet</span>
      The tool has not been switched on. Everything below shows exactly what it will ask
      for and exactly what it will give back — nothing you type here goes anywhere today.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        Goals rarely stall because they are too small. They stall because the first
        move is enormous, public, and embarrassing to get wrong. This tool does one thing:
        it cuts the goal down until the first step fits in twenty minutes and leaves
        something behind that you can point at.
      </p>
      <p class="meta">
        <PageRef page={chapter.data.printedPage} kind={`Chapter ${chapter.data.n} · The Play`} />
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="from-book">
    <h2 id="from-book">The step it automates</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This is not a new idea bolted onto the book. It is the third step of Chapter 1's
        Play, and the whole step reads:
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p><b>{step.n}. {step.title}</b> {step.text}</p>
        <cite>Teen &amp; Grow Rich, printed page {chapter.data.printedPage}</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        You can do it without the tool in about a minute. The tool exists for the days when
        you cannot see how.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="input">
    <h2 id="input">What it asks for</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <div class="field">
        <label class="field__label" for="goal">The goal that feels too big</label>
        <p class="field__hint" id="goal-hint">
          <b class="field__ai">An AI model reads what you type. Nothing is stored.</b>
          One sentence is enough. No names, no school, no address — it does not need them
          and the answer is no better with them in.
        </p>
        <textarea
          id="goal"
          name="goal"
          rows="3"
          disabled
          aria-describedby="goal-hint goal-status"
          placeholder="The tool is not live yet."></textarea>
        <p class="field__status" id="goal-status">
          Disabled until the tool is live. It is disabled rather than hidden so you can see
          the whole thing before you decide whether you would ever use it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="cta" disabled>Shrink it — not live yet</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="output">
    <h2 id="output">What it gives back</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Three steps. Each one fits in twenty minutes, and each one names the proof it
        leaves behind — because proof is the thing the next chapter runs on, and a step
        that leaves nothing behind is a step you cannot tell you took.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* A section rather than a div: an aria-label on a generic element is dropped by
        several screen readers, and this block needs to announce itself as an example. */}
    <section class="result" aria-label="Example of the output. Not advice about your goal.">
      <p class="result__tag">Example output — not advice about your goal</p>
      <p class="result__goal">
        <span class="result__goal-key">Goal typed in</span>
        {EXAMPLE_GOAL}
      </p>

      <ol class="steps">
        {
          EXAMPLE_STEPS.map((s, i) => (
            <li class="step">
              <p class="step__n">{i + 1} · 20 minutes</p>
              <p class="step__do">{s.step}</p>
              <p class="step__proof">
                <span class="step__proof-key">The proof this leaves</span>
                {s.proof}
              </p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>

      <p class="result__action">
        Pick one. Do it before tomorrow night. Keep whatever it produces.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="prose note">
      It never picks for you and it never tells you the goal is wrong. Three options, one
      of which you can start now, is the entire job.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="check">
    <h2 id="check">The Reality Check for this chapter</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Straight from printed page {check.data.printedPage}, in full and unedited.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Box kind="check" class="check">
      {/* Every Reality Check carries its own flag, on every surface that shows one (D12). */}
      {checkMeta && (
        <p class="check__flag">
          <Flag level={checkMeta.flag} size="sm" />
        </p>
      )}
      <p>{check.data.text}</p>
    </Box>
  </section>

  {/* The refusal path has to have a destination that exists whether or not the function
      is ever switched on. Every route below is one the book's own Reality Check for
      threats, sexual messages and blackmail already names.

      There is deliberately NO helpline number or finder link here yet. Inventing one for a
      13-year-old in a bad hour is worse than admitting the gap, so the gap is stated in
      the block below and the routes that do exist are given plainly. See docs/for-ryan.md
      §7 — a verified international finder plus a Dutch one, checked by someone who does
      safeguarding professionally, is pre-launch work. */}
  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="help">
    <h2 id="help">If the thing in the way is not a goal</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        If what is actually stopping you is someone threatening you, someone asking you to
        keep a friendship secret, or how you are feeling about yourself, no twenty-minute
        first step is the right answer to that. None of that gets broken into smaller
        tasks, and it is not something you are supposed to solve on your own.
      </p>

      <div class="pending" aria-labelledby="helpline-h">
        <p class="pending__label" id="helpline-h">Helpline finder — not in place yet</p>
        <p class="pending__note">
          This site does not yet list a helpline you can call or message. One verified
          finder — international, plus one for the Netherlands — is being checked with
          someone who does safeguarding professionally, and it will be added here before
          this site goes live. Making one up in the meantime would be the worse mistake, so
          the routes below are the ones this page can stand behind today. Nothing here is a
          crisis service, including the mailbox in the footer: nobody reads that urgently.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="help">
        <li>
          Tell one adult today — a parent or guardian, a teacher, or your school's
          safeguarding lead. If the first adult does not act, tell a second one.
        </li>
        <li>
          The police, or your local emergency number, if you have been threatened or you
          are frightened for your safety.
        </li>
        <li>
          A family doctor if sleep or eating has changed, and a school counselor is a
          reasonable first stop when the worry is at home.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/reality-check/mindful-tech">
            What to do about threats, sexual messages or blackmail
          </a>, in full. It does not need this tool to be running.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">
        You do not have to work out what is wrong before you tell someone, and you do not
        need the right words ready. Saying “something is going on and I do not know how to
        say it” is a complete sentence and it is enough to start with.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="ai">
    <h2 id="ai">About the AI, plainly</h2>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__key">It is AI</p>
        <p class="row__value">
          Your sentence is read by an AI model, and the three steps come back from that
          model. It can be wrong, and it does not know anything about your situation beyond
          the sentence you typed.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__key">Nothing is stored</p>
        <p class="row__value">
          Not your goal, not the steps, not a log of either. It is sent, answered and
          dropped. There is no account here and nowhere for it to be kept.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__key">It is not a chat</p>
        <p class="row__value">
          One goal in, three steps out. It never writes in Ryan's voice and it never
          generates content from the book.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__key">Some things it will not answer</p>
        <p class="row__value">
          If what you type involves self-harm, abuse, grooming or blackmail, it stops and
          gives one fixed response instead: tell a trusted adult today, and the routes set
          out under <a href="#help">If the thing in the way is not a goal</a> above. It
          will not turn any of that into a twenty-minute task.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__key">If it is down</p>
        <p class="row__value">
          Nothing else on this site stops working. Do it by hand with{" "}
          <a href="/c/01">Chapter 1's Play</a>, or start from{" "}
          <a href="/worksheet/starting-point">Your Starting Point</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  .wrap {
    max-inline-size: 72rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 3rem);
  }

  .prose {
    max-inline-size: var(--container-measure);
  }

  .prose p + p,
  .prose blockquote,
  /* Equal air below the quote as above it, so the site's own words are clearly outside
     the book's. */
  .prose blockquote + p {
    margin-block-start: 0.9em;
  }

  .status {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    max-inline-size: var(--container-measure);
    margin-block-start: 1.75rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    color: var(--text-default);
    background: var(--surface-card);
    /* 3px, not 6px: 6px solid orange is the Your 24-Hour Build signature (design-system
       §3) and this is a page-status note, not a box from the book. The hairline gives it
       an edge in light mode, where --surface-card is the page white. */
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-hairline);
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--accent-dot);
  }

  .status__badge {
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: var(--text-label--letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .lede {
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-subtitle);
    line-height: var(--text-subtitle--line-height);
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .meta {
    margin-block-start: 0.9rem;
  }

  .section {
    margin-block-start: 3rem;
  }

  .section > h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    line-height: var(--text-h2--line-height);
    color: var(--text-section);
    max-inline-size: var(--container-measure);
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: 1rem;
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--accent-spine);
  }

  cite {
    display: block;
    margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .field {
    margin-block-start: 1.25rem;
  }

  .field__label {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: var(--text-label--letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .field__hint,
  .field__status {
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .field__hint {
    margin-block: 0.35rem 0.6rem;
  }

  textarea {
    inline-size: 100%;
    padding: 0.75rem;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    color: var(--text-default);
    background: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--control-edge);
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  textarea:disabled {
    opacity: 1;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    border-style: dashed;
  }

  .field__status {
    margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
  }

  .cta {
    margin-block-start: 1.25rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.2rem;
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 700;
    /* Orange fill takes navy text. White on orange is 2.05:1 and is forbidden. */
    color: var(--cta-text);
    background: var(--cta-fill);
    border: none;
  }

  .cta:disabled {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px dashed var(--rule-hairline);
  }

  .result {
    max-inline-size: var(--container-measure);
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    background: var(--surface-card);
    /* Not --rule-hairline: in light mode --surface-card is the page white, so the border
       is the only thing saying "this is an example, not your answer". A decorative
       hairline at ~1.3:1 cannot carry that. */
    border: 1px solid var(--control-edge);
  }

  .result__tag {
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: var(--text-label--letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .result__goal {
    margin-block-start: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .result__goal-key,
  .step__proof-key {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: var(--text-label--letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .steps {
    margin-block-start: 1.25rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--rule-hairline);
  }

  .step {
    padding-block: 0.9rem;
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--rule-hairline);
  }

  .step__n {
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: var(--text-label--letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    /* Numerals are data. */
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums slashed-zero;
  }

  .step__do {
    margin-block-start: 0.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .step__proof {
    margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
  }

  .result__action {
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .check {
    margin-block-start: 1.25rem;
  }

  .check__flag {
    margin-block-end: 0.6rem;
  }

  .field__ai {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  /* Dashed, the same shape /get uses for a thing that is genuinely not built yet. A solid
     card would read as an answer; this has to read as a missing one. */
  .pending {
    margin-block-start: 1.1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    background: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px dashed var(--rule-hairline);
  }

  .pending__label {
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: var(--text-label--letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .pending__note {
    margin-block-start: 0.35rem;
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .help {
    margin-block-start: 0.9rem;
    padding-inline-start: 1.1rem;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .help li {
    position: relative;
    margin-block-start: 0.45rem;
  }

  .help li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: -1.1rem;
    inset-block-start: 0.62em;
    inline-size: 0.5rem;
    block-size: 2px;
    background: var(--accent-spine);
  }

  .rows {
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--rule-hairline);
  }

  .row {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.2rem 2rem;
    padding-block: 0.9rem;
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--rule-hairline);
  }

  .row__key {
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .row__value {
    max-inline-size: var(--container-measure);
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 12rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: baseline;
    }
  }

  .note {
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  a {
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent-spine);
  }
</style>
